    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4437" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aucŭpātōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>belonging to</i>, or <i>useful in
			bird-catching</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harundo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 36, 66, § 172</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cum anno permansit inundatio, proficiunt in
					aucupatoriam amplitudinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 36, 66, § 169</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calami,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					14, 218</span></i>
			; Plin. l. l.</div>
